% algebras via generalized hep-derivors), also read by doc-gen4 for the citations
% in the docstrings of the library.
%
% Citation keys follow a single scheme: the surname of the first author
% followed by the four-digit year (Burmeister1986); with two authors, both
% surnames (BarrWells2012); with three or more, the first surname and EtAl
% (AraEtAl2025). Spanish double surnames contribute only the first one
% (ClimentCosme2019); accents are dropped and particles kept (Godel1931,
% MacLane1998, deMouraUllrich2021); undated items use ND; corporate authors
% use a short name (Mathlib2020); clashes get a, b, c, ... in file order.
%
% The entries were contrasted (October 2026) with external records: Crossref
% for journal articles, chapters and proceedings; the arXiv abstract pages for
% preprints; DataCite for the Zenodo DOIs; and, for web pages, that the URL
% resolves.
%
% No online record could be matched for the following entries, which are kept
% as they were (up to evident typos): AndrekaNemeti1983, Benabou1968,
